.TH "ODFFIELDAUDIT" "1" "2026-11-14" "odfpy" "User commands"
.SH NAME
odffieldaudit \- audit user-field declarations, references and cached display text in an ODF file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B odffieldaudit
.RB [ \-f
.IR field ]...
.RB [ \-j ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-only-issues ]
.IR path " ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B odffieldaudit
reports where a user field is really used in an OpenDocument package.
Only genuine field references
.RI ( text:user-field-get
and
.IR text:user-field-input )
are reported; ordinary body text that merely spells the same value is
not a reference and is never listed.
.PP
For every field the program shows its declarations
.RI ( text:user-field-decl )
with the declared value type and value, and every reference together
with the display text cached inside the reference element. Office
applications only refresh that cached text when fields are updated, so
a string field whose cached text differs from its declared value is
flagged as stale. For non-string fields (numbers, dates, booleans) a
difference is reported as display-differs, because it may simply result
from number or date formatting.
.PP
References whose name has no matching declaration in the same document
scope are listed as undeclared references. Each embedded object (the
Object N folders, including nested objects) is an independent document,
so a field inside an object is resolved against that object's own
declarations only, never against the host document.
.PP
Every reported occurrence carries a location of the form
.IR part : line : column
that points at the opening tag of the element, for example
.IR styles.xml:11:11
for a field used in a page header.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " field"
Restrict the audit to the named user field. May be given more than once.
By default all user fields are audited.
.TP
.B \-j
.TQ
.B \-\-json
Emit machine readable JSON instead of the human readable text report.
.TP
.B \-\-only-issues
Only list undeclared references and references whose cached display text
differs from the declared value.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The program exits with status 1 when at least one undeclared reference
or stale string field was found, and 0 otherwise. Non-string
display-differs findings do not change the exit status on their own.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.nf
.RS
odffieldaudit \-f 批号 document.odt
odffieldaudit \-\-json \-\-only-issues document.odt
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR odfuserfield (1)
